1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,240
My mother swore this brass pendant would measure my lifespan. But she lied to me.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:13,860
Today the numbers froze at zero. Not mine. The old man across the street stopped moving entirely.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:20,880
I ran outside and screamed his name. The moment I confessed my terror, the numbers jumped back up.

4
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:27,636
That is when the terrible truth clawed its way into my throat. This glass does not track time.

5
00:00:27,936 --> 00:00:34,512
It measures how much borrowed breath remains in the world before my next dishonesty steals it.

6
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:42,564
Every small white lie I tell buys a stranger another hour. Total honesty brings instant death.

7
00:00:42,864 --> 00:00:50,016
I told my best friend she looked amazing yesterday. Instantly, a dying child in the hospital woke up.

8
00:00:50,316 --> 00:00:57,756
So I started lying constantly. To everyone. About everything. Just to keep the fragile world breathing.

9
00:00:58,056 --> 00:01:06,744
My entire existence is now a manufactured fiction keeping strangers alive. I am a machine of deceit.

10
00:01:07,044 --> 00:01:13,884
The pendant glows bright gold in my trembling hand. How many lives did your last truth just buy?
